---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Team screen
// (project/AdminTeam.dc.html / AdminTeamDark.dc.html -> NavSidebar
// role="admin" active="Team" + the shared NavTop.astro (section="Manage"
// page="Team") + PageUsers, imported with role="admin" — a single
// component parameterized for both the Admin ("Team") and Super Admin
// ("Users") variants, same dc-import pattern already seen on Admin Ticket
// Detail's PageAdminTicket) — this REPLACES the old AppShell/DESIGN.md
// staff page that used to live at this same route (/admin/staff,
// unchanged), same "redesign in place, don't fork a second URL" precedent
// already used for /admin (Admin Dashboard). NavSidebar's "Team" item now
// links here (see that file's own header comment).
//
// PERMISSIONS: unchanged — /admin/staff is already gated to
// admin/super_admin by src/middleware.ts, not touched this turn. Every
// authorization boundary below is a direct port of what the old page
// already enforced (both client-side and, authoritatively, server-side
// inside create_approval_request()/updateStaffProfile's RLS) — nothing was
// loosened or invented:
//  - A row whose real role is super_admin is always "Protected account",
//    for EITHER viewer role — the old page enforced this uniformly
//    (`isProtected = p.role === "super_admin"`), matching your explicit
//    "Do NOT allow creation of another super_admin through the normal Team
//    UI" / "preserve the existing hierarchy" instructions. Another
//    super_admin cannot be deactivated or role-changed from here by
//    anyone, including a fellow super_admin.
//  - Your own row is always "This is you" — no self-service
//    deactivate/role-change from this screen.
//  - super_admin viewing any other (non-protected, non-self) row: direct
//    Deactivate/Reactivate + role-change via the unmodified
//    updateStaffProfile action (RLS-backed, not approval-gated — this is
//    the real "unrestricted staff management" capability super_admin
//    already had).
//  - admin viewing any other (non-protected, non-self) row: "Request
//    deactivation" / "Request role change" via the unmodified
//    requestApproval RPC wrapper (create_approval_request, action types
//    deactivate_staff/change_role) — exactly the real Phase 9 approval
//    gate, reviewed at /admin/approvals. Admin never gets direct mutation
//    power over another staff account merely because the design shows a
//    single unified table — that capability line is drawn server-side
//    (updateStaffProfile relies on RLS scoped to super_admin only; an
//    admin calling it against another profile affects 0 rows) and was not
//    touched.
//  - Invite: both admin and super_admin get the exact same real
//    inviteStaff capability (already authorized for both, confirmed by
//    reading the action before building anything) — role restricted to
//    sales_staff/inventory_staff/admin, never super_admin (a closed zod
//    enum on the action itself, not just a UI restriction).
//
// NO-FABRICATION DECISIONS — the design's sample data invents an entire
// "internal social network" of fields that do not exist in this schema.
// Every one was checked against the real `profiles` table (id, role,
// full_name, phone, avatar_url, is_active, created_at, updated_at — no
// email column) before deciding how to handle it:
//  - Email: auth.users.email is not exposed to the app for anyone other
//    than the signed-in user's own session — customer_contact_email()
//    (the one function that reads auth.users) explicitly returns null for
//    a non-customer target (checked its source directly). The old
//    /admin/staff page already reflected this by never displaying email at
//    all; that omission is preserved here, not newly invented.
//  - "2FA" column: no MFA/2FA system exists anywhere in this Supabase Auth
//    setup — omitted entirely, not disabled-with-a-title (a wholly
//    nonexistent concept, same "full omission" precedent as Category on
//    Support Tickets/Products).
//  - "Last active" column: no login/activity timestamp is tracked or
//    exposed anywhere in this app — omitted entirely. Explicitly listed in
//    your own instructions as something never to fabricate.
//  - "Joined" (super variant) / "This month" business-activity metrics
//    (admin variant, e.g. "38 orders · ₹24.6L", "14 receipts · 6
//    adjustments"): the business-metric version is entirely fabricated —
//    no per-staff performance rollup exists. Replaced for BOTH viewer
//    roles with the one genuinely real, always-available equivalent:
//    profiles.created_at, labeled "Joined" — an honest substitution of a
//    real field for the design's intended (but here fake) semantic, same
//    "relabel to match real semantics" precedent as inventory_value_
//    summary's "at price" relabel.
//  - Status ("Active"/"Invited"/"Suspended"): profiles has exactly one
//    real status signal, the is_active boolean — "Invited" (would require
//    reading auth.users.last_sign_in_at, a new capability) and "Suspended"
//    (no distinct value from "deactivated") were dropped; real rows render
//    only Active/Inactive, matching the old page's own two-state Badge.
//  - Checkboxes + bulk "Change role…" footer action: no real bulk mutation
//    action exists — omitted, same precedent as every other Admin list
//    screen.
//  - Import CSV / Export / "View" toggle: no real capability behind any of
//    these — omitted entirely, never stubbed as fake-disabled buttons
//    (these aren't even honestly-real-but-unavailable concepts, they're
//    pure design flourishes with zero backend counterpart).
//  - Pagination ("Page 1 of 6", rows-per-page): real dataset is a handful
//    of staff rows — replaced with a real "{N} of {M} people" count
//    footer, same precedent as every other Admin list screen.
//  - The design's isAdmin banner claims "You can invite Sales staff and
//    Inventory staff only" — checked against the real inviteStaff action
//    and found this to be simply WRONG for this app: admin is actually
//    authorized to invite Admin too (never Super admin). Copying the
//    design's incorrect claim verbatim would misrepresent a real
//    capability, so the banner text was corrected to state the real
//    allowed roles instead of reproducing inaccurate design copy.
//  - Stats row: the design shows different fabricated stats per role
//    variant ("Active this week … of 46", "Pending invites … expires in 7
//    days" — no activity-tracking or invitation-status data exists for
//    either). Replaced with 5 real cards, real for BOTH viewer roles:
//    Super admins / Admins / Sales staff / Inventory staff (real per-role
//    counts) / Inactive (real is_active = false count). "Customers" (the
//    super variant's 5th card) was left out — already has its own real
//    page (/admin/customers).
//  - Row "…" overflow-menu button: replaced with the same inline
//    real-controls pattern the old page already used (visible
//    button(s)/select, not a hidden menu) — a menu implies more options
//    than genuinely exist here, and every other Admin list screen in this
//    project already favors direct visible controls over a disclosure
//    menu for real per-row actions.
//  - Search: design says "Filter by name or email" — narrowed to name only
//    (no real email field to search).
//  - Role/Status toolbar facets: real, functional — same dashed-pill
//    facet-select pattern already established on Admin Support Tickets'
//    "+ Status"/"+ Assignee", driving real `role`/`status` query params.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";

const userId = Astro.locals.user!.id;
const isSuperAdmin = Astro.locals.role === "super_admin";
const viewerRole = (isSuperAdmin ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

const url = Astro.url;
const search = url.searchParams.get("search")?.trim() ?? "";
const roleFilter = url.searchParams.get("role") ?? "";
const statusFilter = url.searchParams.get("status") ?? "";
const invited = url.searchParams.get("invited");

const { data: staffRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("profiles")
  .select("id, full_name, role, is_active, created_at")
  .neq("role", "customer")
  .order("role")
  .order("full_name");

const ROLE_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
  super_admin: "Super admin",
  admin: "Admin",
  sales_staff: "Sales staff",
  inventory_staff: "Inventory staff",
};
const ROLE_TONE: Record<string, "solid" | "info" | "outline" | "muted"> = {
  super_admin: "solid",
  admin: "info",
  sales_staff: "outline",
  inventory_staff: "muted",
};
const ALL_ROLES = ["super_admin", "admin", "sales_staff", "inventory_staff"] as const;
const INVITE_ROLE_OPTIONS = ["sales_staff", "inventory_staff", "admin"] as const;

const allRows = (staffRows ?? []).map((p) => ({
  id: p.id as string,
  name: (p.full_name as string | null) ?? "Unnamed",
  role: p.role as string,
  isActive: p.is_active as boolean,
  createdAt: p.created_at as string,
  isSelf: p.id === userId,
  isProtected: p.role === "super_admin",
}));

const filtered = allRows.filter((r) => {
  if (roleFilter && r.role !== roleFilter) return false;
  if (statusFilter === "active" && !r.isActive) return false;
  if (statusFilter === "inactive" && r.isActive) return false;
  if (search && !r.name.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase())) return false;
  return true;
});

function buildUrl(overrides: Record<string, string | undefined>) {
  const next = new URLSearchParams(url.search);
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(overrides)) {
    if (value) next.set(key, value);
    else next.delete(key);
  }
  const qs = next.toString();
  return qs ? `/admin/staff?${qs}` : "/admin/staff";
}

function initials(name: string): string {
  const parts = name.split(" ").filter(Boolean).slice(0, 2).map((p) => p[0]!.toUpperCase());
  return parts.length > 0 ? parts.join("") : "—";
}
function fmtJoined(iso: string): string {
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { month: "short", year: "numeric" });
}

const stats = [
  { label: "Super admins", value: allRows.filter((r) => r.role === "super_admin").length, note: viewerRole === "super_admin" ? "incl. you" : "" },
  { label: "Admins", value: allRows.filter((r) => r.role === "admin").length, note: viewerRole === "admin" ? "incl. you" : "" },
  { label: "Sales staff", value: allRows.filter((r) => r.role === "sales_staff").length, note: "" },
  { label: "Inventory staff", value: allRows.filter((r) => r.role === "inventory_staff").length, note: "" },
  { label: "Inactive", value: allRows.filter((r) => !r.isActive).length, note: `of ${allRows.length}` },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Team — Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Team" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Manage" page="Team" />

      <main id="main-content" class="tm__main">
        <div class="tm__header">
          <div class="tm__heading-col">
            <h1>Team</h1>
            <span class="tm__subtitle">{allRows.length} people · Customer accounts are managed in Customers</span>
          </div>
          <button type="button" id="tm-invite-toggle" class="tm__btn tm__btn--primary">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" /></svg>
            Invite staff
          </button>
        </div>

        {invited && (
          <p class="tm__banner" role="status">
            Invitation sent.
          </p>
        )}

        <section id="tm-invite-panel" class="tm__invite-panel" hidden aria-label="Invite staff">
          <h2>Invite staff</h2>
          <span class="tm__invite-hint">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 18 0a9 9 0 1 0-18 0M12 11v5M12 8h.01" /></svg>
            You can invite Sales staff, Inventory staff, or Admin — not Super admin.
          </span>
          <form id="tm-invite-form" class="tm__invite-form">
            <div class="tm__field-col">
              <label for="tm-invite-name">Full name</label>
              <input type="text" id="tm-invite-name" name="fullName" required />
            </div>
            <div class="tm__field-col">
              <label for="tm-invite-email">Email</label>
              <input type="email" id="tm-invite-email" name="email" required />
            </div>
            <div class="tm__field-col">
              <label for="tm-invite-role">Role</label>
              <select id="tm-invite-role" name="role" required>
                {INVITE_ROLE_OPTIONS.map((r) => (
                  <option value={r}>{ROLE_LABEL[r]}</option>
                ))}
              </select>
            </div>
            <p id="tm-invite-message" class="tm__form-message" role="status" />
            <div class="tm__invite-actions">
              <button type="button" id="tm-invite-cancel" class="tm__btn">Cancel</button>
              <button type="submit" class="tm__btn tm__btn--primary">Send invitation</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        </section>

        <div class="tm__stats">
          {stats.map((s) => (
            <div class="tm__stat-card">
              <span class="tm__stat-label">{s.label}</span>
              <div class="tm__stat-body">
                <span class="tm__stat-value">{s.value}</span>
                {s.note && <span class="tm__stat-note">{s.note}</span>}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="tm__toolbar">
          <form method="get" action="/admin/staff" class="tm__search-form">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 11a7 7 0 1 0 14 0a7 7 0 1 0-14 0M20 20l-4-4"></path></svg>
            <input type="search" name="search" value={search} aria-label="Filter by name" placeholder="Filter by name…" class="tm__search-input" />
            {roleFilter && <input type="hidden" name="role" value={roleFilter} />}
            {statusFilter && <input type="hidden" name="status" value={statusFilter} />}
          </form>

          <select id="tm-role-filter" class="tm__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by role">
            <option value={buildUrl({ role: undefined })} selected={!roleFilter}>+ Role</option>
            {ALL_ROLES.map((r) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ role: r })} selected={roleFilter === r}>{ROLE_LABEL[r]}</option>
            ))}
          </select>

          <select id="tm-status-filter" class="tm__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by status">
            <option value={buildUrl({ status: undefined })} selected={!statusFilter}>+ Status</option>
            <option value={buildUrl({ status: "active" })} selected={statusFilter === "active"}>Active</option>
            <option value={buildUrl({ status: "inactive" })} selected={statusFilter === "inactive"}>Inactive</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        {
          filtered.length > 0 ? (
            <div class="tm__panel">
              <div class="tm__grid tm__grid-head">
                <span>User</span>
                <span>Role</span>
                <span>Joined</span>
                <span>Status</span>
                <span>Actions</span>
              </div>
              {filtered.map((r) => (
                <div class="tm__grid tm__row" data-profile-id={r.id} data-current-role={r.role}>
                  <span class="tm__user-cell">
                    <span class="tm__avatar">{initials(r.name)}</span>
                    <span class="tm__user-name">{r.name}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span><span class={`tm__pill tm__pill--${ROLE_TONE[r.role] ?? "muted"}`}>{ROLE_LABEL[r.role] ?? r.role}</span></span>
                  <span class="tm__muted-cell">{fmtJoined(r.createdAt)}</span>
                  <span><span class={`tm__pill tm__pill--${r.isActive ? "active" : "inactive"}`}>{r.isActive ? "Active" : "Inactive"}</span></span>
                  <span class="tm__actions-cell">
                    {r.isProtected ? (
                      <span class="tm__muted-cell">Protected account</span>
                    ) : r.isSelf ? (
                      <span class="tm__muted-cell">This is you</span>
                    ) : isSuperAdmin ? (
                      <div class="tm__row-controls">
                        <button type="button" class="tm-toggle-active tm__link-btn" data-next-active={(!r.isActive).toString()}>
                          {r.isActive ? "Deactivate" : "Reactivate"}
                        </button>
                        <select class="tm-role-select tm__mini-select" aria-label={`Change role for ${r.name}`}>
                          {INVITE_ROLE_OPTIONS.map((opt) => (
                            <option value={opt} selected={opt === r.role}>{ROLE_LABEL[opt]}</option>
                          ))}
                        </select>
                        <button type="button" class="tm-save-role tm__link-btn">Save role</button>
                      </div>
                    ) : (
                      <div class="tm__row-controls">
                        {r.isActive && (
                          <button type="button" class="tm-request-deactivate tm__link-btn">Request deactivation</button>
                        )}
                        <select class="tm-role-select tm__mini-select" aria-label={`Change role for ${r.name}`}>
                          {INVITE_ROLE_OPTIONS.map((opt) => (
                            <option value={opt} selected={opt === r.role}>{ROLE_LABEL[opt]}</option>
                          ))}
                        </select>
                        <button type="button" class="tm-request-role tm__link-btn">Request role change</button>
                      </div>
                    )}
                    <p class="tm-row-message tm__row-message" role="status" />
                  </span>
                </div>
              ))}
              <div class="tm__panel-footer">{filtered.length} of {allRows.length} people</div>
            </div>
          ) : (
            <div class="tm__empty">
              <p class="tm__empty-title">No one found</p>
              <p class="tm__empty-body">Try a different search or filter.</p>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sd {
    --sd-shell: #fafafa;
    --sd-panel: #ffffff;
    --sd-card: #ffffff;
    --sd-fg: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-fg2: #404040;
    --sd-muted: #f5f5f5;
    --sd-muted-fg: #737373;
    --sd-border: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-input: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-primary: #171717;
    --sd-primary-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-success-bg: #ecfdf3;
    --sd-success-fg: #15803d;
    --sd-warn-bg: #fef3e2;
    --sd-warn-fg: #9a3412;
    --sd-danger-bg: #feecec;
    --sd-danger-fg: #b91c1c;
    --sd-info-bg: #eef2ff;
    --sd-info-fg: #3538cd;
    --sd-accent: #2b50e0;
    --sd-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    color-scheme: light;

    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font-family: "Geist", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sd[data-theme="dark"] {
    --sd-shell: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-panel: #0f0f0f;
    --sd-card: #171717;
    --sd-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-fg2: #d4d4d4;
    --sd-muted: #262626;
    --sd-muted-fg: #a3a3a3;
    --sd-border: #262626;
    --sd-input: #363636;
    --sd-primary: #fafafa;
    --sd-primary-fg: #171717;
    --sd-success-bg: #0f2a1c;
    --sd-success-fg: #4ade80;
    --sd-warn-bg: #2e1f0e;
    --sd-warn-fg: #fdba74;
    --sd-danger-bg: #2d1414;
    --sd-danger-fg: #f87171;
    --sd-info-bg: #1e2240;
    --sd-info-fg: #a5b4fc;
    --sd-accent: #6b8afb;
    --sd-shadow: none;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
  .sd__backdrop {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    z-index: 20;
  }
  .sd__sidebar {
    height: 100vh;
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__sidebar {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      z-index: 30;
      transform: translateX(-100%);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .sd__sidebar.is-open {
      transform: translateX(0);
    }
    .sd__backdrop.is-open {
      display: block;
    }
  }
  .sd__panel {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 8px 8px 8px 0;
    background: var(--sd-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__panel {
      margin: 8px;
    }
  }

  .tm__main {
    flex-grow: 1;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 24px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .tm__main {
      padding: 16px;
    }
  }

  .tm__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tm__heading-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .tm__heading-col h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .tm__subtitle {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tm__banner {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-success-fg);
  }

  .tm__btn {
    height: 36px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 14px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    background: var(--sd-card);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .tm__btn--primary {
    border: 0;
    background: var(--sd-primary);
    color: var(--sd-primary-fg);
  }

  .tm__invite-panel {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .tm__invite-panel h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .tm__invite-hint {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    height: 30px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--sd-info-bg);
    color: var(--sd-info-fg);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    width: fit-content;
  }
  .tm__invite-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 420px;
  }
  .tm__field-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .tm__field-col label {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .tm__field-col input,
  .tm__field-col select {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    height: 36px;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--sd-fg);
  }
  .tm__invite-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .tm__form-message {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-danger-fg);
    min-height: 0;
  }

  .tm__stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
